  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Other Management Consulting Services (NAICS 541618) obligations are $138M for FY2026 to date. Awarding activity includes 520 awards and an average award size of $265K. Obligations fell 83.7% year over year. Annual history shows a peak at $1.3B in FY24, with prior totals of $537M in FY21, $913M in FY22, $864M in FY23, and $843M in FY25. Buying in FY2026 to date concentrates in a few agencies: the Department of Defense obligated $46.9M and the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $44.1M, followed by the Department of State at $18.1M. Vendor concentration is also evident: ISLAND PEER REVIEW ORGANIZATION INC received $52.4M and PALANTIR USG INC received $22M. The FY2026 to date totals are partial because the fiscal year remains in progress. This snapshot shows a much smaller current-year run rate compared with recent full fiscal years and highlights which agencies and vendors account for the bulk of obligations so far.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How steep was the year-over-year change in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 83.7% year over year. FY26 obligations are $138M compared with $843M in FY25 and $1.3B in FY24, showing a much lower current-year run rate. The count of awards is 520 and the average award size is $265K, which reflect the current-year activity mix. The FY2026 total is partial because the fiscal year is not complete."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $46.9M and the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $44.1M, making them the top buyers. The Department of State obligated $18.1M and the Department of Energy obligated $12.9M, with remaining top buyers at lower amounts. ISLAND PEER REVIEW ORGANIZATION INC received $52.4M and PALANTIR USG INC received $22M, making them the largest vendors so far."
      }
    ]
  },
